# Fix tickets means the support button

When Alec says "fix tickets," the work is the trouble tickets filed from the GP terminal support button. Do not start with GitHub issues.

Look here, in this order:

1. `GET /api/support/agent-inbox` and `GET /api/support/tickets` (GP auth or `x-support-agent-token`). Table: `support_tickets`.
2. Each ticket's `description` plus its screenshot: `GET /api/support/tickets/{id}/screenshot`.
3. Settings → Support tickets, which reads the same table.

The button posts `description` and a page snapshot (`screenshot_b64`) to `POST /api/support/tickets`. Code is `api/domains/support_tickets.py`. The button UI is `web/gp-app/src/components/support/SupportFab.tsx`.

Read the description and look at the snapshot before editing. Fix his open reports. If a previous session already started that fix, continue it. Do not revert unrelated dirty files.

Do not push or deploy unless he asks. Mark a ticket fixed only after the change is in the tree he asked to ship.
